# Turkish puts the daypart adverbial in FRONT of the time phrase it scopes:
# "öğleden sonra saat üç" is the plain way to say three in the afternoon, and
# TDK carries the mirror compound "akşam saati" (zarf, = akşamleyin) with the
# daypart word leading the hour noun (Güncel Türkçe Sözlük, s.v. "akşam",
# https://sozluk.gov.tr/). The postposed order occurs too, so the clock
# construction reads the marker on either side of the hour.
akşam
öğleden sonra
